  "content": {
    "id": "p16-g76-87-root",
    "type": "question",
    "label": null,
    "prompt": "Write down the values of $\\theta\\in[0^\\circ,360^\\circ]$ so that the following are equal.",
    "layout": "grid",
    "columns": 2,
    "questionDiagrams": [],
    "children": [
      {
        "id": "p16-g76-87-a",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "a",
        "prompt": "$\\sin20^\\circ=\\sin\\theta$",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "$20^\\circ,\\ 160^\\circ$",
          "worked": "The given angle is $20^\\circ$. Sine has equal $y$-coordinates at supplementary angles.\n$$\\begin{align*}\\theta&=180^\\circ-20^\\circ\\\\\\theta&=160^\\circ\\end{align*}$$\nThus $\\theta=20^\\circ,160^\\circ$.",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 8
      },
      {
        "id": "p16-g76-87-b",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "b",
        "prompt": "$\\cos70^\\circ=\\cos\\theta$",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "$70^\\circ,\\ 290^\\circ$",
          "worked": "The given angle is $70^\\circ$. Reflection across the $x$-axis preserves the cosine value.\n$$\\begin{align*}\\theta&=360^\\circ-70^\\circ\\\\\\theta&=290^\\circ\\end{align*}$$\nThus $\\theta=70^\\circ,290^\\circ$.",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 8
      },
      {
        "id": "p16-g76-87-c",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "c",
        "prompt": "$\\tan15^\\circ=\\tan\\theta$",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "$15^\\circ,\\ 195^\\circ$",
          "worked": "The given angle is $15^\\circ$. A half-turn preserves the ray's gradient and hence its tangent value.\n$$\\begin{align*}\\theta&=180^\\circ+15^\\circ\\\\\\theta&=195^\\circ\\end{align*}$$\nThus $\\theta=15^\\circ,195^\\circ$.",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 8
      },
      {
        "id": "p16-g76-87-d",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "d",
        "prompt": "$\\sin95^\\circ=\\sin\\theta$",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "$95^\\circ,\\ 85^\\circ$",
          "worked": "The given angle is $95^\\circ$. Sine has equal $y$-coordinates at supplementary angles.\n$$\\begin{align*}\\theta&=180^\\circ-95^\\circ\\\\\\theta&=85^\\circ\\end{align*}$$\nThus $\\theta=95^\\circ,85^\\circ$.",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 8
      },
      {
        "id": "p16-g76-87-e",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "e",
        "prompt": "$\\cos125^\\circ=\\cos\\theta$",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "$125^\\circ,\\ 235^\\circ$",
          "worked": "The given angle is $125^\\circ$. Reflection across the $x$-axis preserves the cosine value.\n$$\\begin{align*}\\theta&=360^\\circ-125^\\circ\\\\\\theta&=235^\\circ\\end{align*}$$\nThus $\\theta=125^\\circ,235^\\circ$.",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 8
      },
      {
        "id": "p16-g76-87-f",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "f",
        "prompt": "$\\tan160^\\circ=\\tan\\theta$",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "$160^\\circ,\\ 340^\\circ$",
          "worked": "The given angle is $160^\\circ$. A half-turn preserves the ray's gradient and hence its tangent value.\n$$\\begin{align*}\\theta&=160^\\circ+180^\\circ\\\\\\theta&=340^\\circ\\end{align*}$$\nThus $\\theta=160^\\circ,340^\\circ$.",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 8
      },
      {
        "id": "p16-g76-87-g",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "g",
        "prompt": "$\\sin250^\\circ=\\sin\\theta$",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "$250^\\circ,\\ 290^\\circ$",
          "worked": "The given angle is $250^\\circ$. Its related angle is $70^\\circ$; the fourth-quadrant angle has the same negative $y$-coordinate.\n$$\\begin{align*}\\theta&=360^\\circ-(250^\\circ-180^\\circ)\\\\\\theta&=290^\\circ\\end{align*}$$\nThus $\\theta=250^\\circ,290^\\circ$.",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 8
      },
      {
        "id": "p16-g76-87-h",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "h",
        "prompt": "$\\cos220^\\circ=\\cos\\theta$",
